V-ROW: NEW · S02 · t_b4187218 (ARCH(S02)) · Recommended default: `pnpm pes:accept-hosted` exits 0 on PASS, FAIL and UNVERIFIED alike and carries its verdict on the LAST stdout line, because pnpm 11.20.0 appends `[ELIFECYCLE] Command failed with exit code 1.` to stdout after any script that exits non-zero (`probes/ARCH-PES-S02/pnpm-streams.out`, measured 2026-09-25). That would make SPEC-v3 §5 step 8's second sentence ("A failing run's last line begins `PES-S02-ACCEPT: FAIL `") false on every failing run. Smallest yes/no for V: "Keep the acceptance's exit code at 0 on every outcome, so its last line is always the verdict, as step 8 says?" · VERDICT: yes / CONFIDENCE: medium / STRONGEST COUNTER: a non-zero exit is the universal failure signal, so `pnpm pes:accept-hosted && echo ok` prints `ok` on a FAIL run. The alternative (exit 1 on FAIL) keeps that signal, and step 8's FAIL line is then followed by pnpm's own notice.

