| 2026-09-25 | B1: which Node function is the ONE `deps.lookup`, and how does row 3 call it? | The callback `lookup` of `import { lookup } from "node:dns";`. Row 3 calls it through the module-private `resolveAll(lookup, hostname)` (a `new Promise` around the callback, `{ all: true }`); `https.request` and `tls.connect` receive the same value untouched. | One value, one call shape: the stub of the suites and the default travel the same path. Measured `probes/ARCH-FIX-PES-S02-p2/b1-lookup-shapes.out`: `node:dns` `lookup` → `127.0.0.1,::1` through `resolveAll`, `status=200` through `https.request`, `authorized=true` through `tls.connect`; the p1 call without a callback throws `ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE`. | ARCH-FIX-PES-S02-p2 (finding B1 of ARCH-REV-PES-S02-p1) |
| 2026-09-25 | B1 alternative: `dns.promises.lookup` as `deps.lookup` (what the feasibility spike calls). | REJECTED. | Passed to `https.request` it never calls back: `req-timeout` (M2), and through `resolveAll` it never settles (M3). `tsc` ACCEPTS it as a `LookupFunction` (`b1-tsc-mutant.out`), so S02-S18 carries two `node:dns` greps as the mechanical guard. | ARCH-FIX-PES-S02-p2 |
| 2026-09-25 | B1 alternative: `util.promisify(deps.lookup)` for the pre-check (the verdict's suggested repair). | REJECTED in favour of the explicit `resolveAll`. | `promisify` of `node:dns` `lookup` dispatches to that function's `util.promisify.custom`, a different code path from the one the stub takes, so the suites would not exercise the default's path. `resolveAll` calls both through the same callback. Both reach the same result on the measured inputs; the choice is the shared path. | ARCH-FIX-PES-S02-p2 |
| 2026-09-25 | B1: how are the suites' lookups written? | One module-private `callbackLookup(answer)` factory, byte-identical in `acceptance/pes-s02-fake-vendor.test.ts` (S02-S13) and `acceptance/pes-s02-hosted.test.ts` (S02-S17); every stub in both files is built by it. It is not exported from a production module, so the 12-name and 7-name export gates are unchanged. | The p1 text described the stub both as "answering" (a return value) and as "calling back"; the factory fixes one shape. The factory text is the text the probe typechecked and ran (G2–G4, G6, G7, G9). | ARCH-FIX-PES-S02-p2 |
| 2026-09-25 | N1: what does dev-api-environment read at the §3 RED event, and is S02-S03 (b) rewritten to fail there? | 10 passed / 2 failed. (b) is NOT rewritten. | (b) expects `DEV_API_ENVIRONMENT_DRIFT`, which base already throws (`apps/runner/src/dev-api-environment.ts:284-287`) on both of its variants before S02-S05; after S02-S06 the new predicate refuses them. The final pair `11:1` is unchanged. | ARCH-FIX-PES-S02-p2 (finding N1 of ARCH-REV-PES-S02-p1) |
| 2026-09-25 | N2: the single-quoted JSON mock body in S02-S04 (ii) step 3. | Labelled EXACT, citing `tests/integration/dev-api-process.test.ts:213`. The self-check's JSON-label regex now matches any `{"` (it matched only a backtick-opened literal and missed this one, `selfcheck6-mutant.out`). | Every other JSON example in the plan is labelled; the narrow regex was the cause. | ARCH-FIX-PES-S02-p2 (finding N2 of ARCH-REV-PES-S02-p1) |
| 2026-09-25 | CORRECTION to the row above "B1 alternative: `util.promisify(deps.lookup)`". | The choice (`resolveAll`) stands; that row's REASON is withdrawn. | Measured after writing it (`probes/ARCH-FIX-PES-S02-p2/b1-promisify.out`): `node:dns` `lookup` has no `util.promisify.custom` on node v26.9.0, and `promisify` resolves `[{"address":"127.0.0.1","family":4},{"address":"::1","family":6}]` (EXACT) for it and the stub's own array for the stub, so the verdict's repair works equally. `resolveAll` is kept because its exact text is the text the probe typechecked and ran (G1–G4), and it types the answer as `LookupAddress[]` in one place. | ARCH-FIX-PES-S02-p2 |

